For a lavaan extention I am currently building, it would be conventient to do the following.

If there is a fit object that contains results for multiple groups, extract a fit object that looks like a single group object for a particular group. So, something like this:

HS.model <- ' visual =~ x1 + x2 + x3  <https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html#cb11-2> textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6  <https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html#cb11-3> speed =~ x7 + x8 + x9 '  <https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html#cb11-4>  <https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html#cb11-5># configural invariance  <https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html#cb11-6>fit1 <- cfa(HS.model, data = HolzingerSwineford1939, group = "school")

## new function
fit2 <- extractGroup(fit1, group = 1)

fit2 should then look like as if HS.model was only fit one group 1. So, don't look like a multiple group model.

Is that possible?

